From ec55c605bcc7dede8f2f3d0b2fb09133d43a4e70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:43:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Lock screen with a PIN: dslock, locks when the lid closes,
 Start > Lock

docs/SLEEP-LOCK-PLAN.md step 4, as the user chose: a PIN, and the
desktop still logs in by itself at boot (no lock at start).
- dslock (Nano-X, on the card): a full-screen window above everything
  (taskbar included), clock and date, the PIN as dots, a 3x4 keypad;
  digits from the touch keyboard or the keypad; wrong PINs wait 1, 2,
  4 ... 30 s; stays on top and keeps the keyboard. "dslock set" sets,
  changes (old PIN first) or removes (empty new PIN) the PIN. Stored as
  an MD5 crypt() hash with a random salt in /home/.lockpin (0600).
- screensleep.c: /proc/dslid "lid=open|closed closes=N" (no ARM7
  request); dsdesk polls it about every second and starts dslock on a
  new close when a PIN is set. Start menu: Lock (above Exit desktop).
- Settings: "Lock PIN" button (dslock set).
Checked in the PC test bed: set a PIN (too short refused, twice), lock,
wrong PIN keeps it locked, the right PIN unlocks, keypad clicks work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
